# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
#
# Runs build/hello.elf in Renode the way the bootloader starts it: the ELF
# loaded at its physical addresses, the E51 and U54_2..4 held halted, U54_1
# started in M-mode at the physical entry 0x0800_0000 (_start_pa; LoadELF
# itself sets the virtual e_entry) with a0 = hart id. Start Renode in the
# project root:
#
#   renode -e "include @renode/hello.resc"
#
# then 'start'. Symbols are virtual (0xFFFFFFC0_08...) but sysbus reads
# physical addresses: subtract 0xFFFFFFC0_00000000 from the symbol's address,
# e.g. g_count at 0xffffffc008003160 is
#
#   sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x08003160
#
# (the low 32 bits). It goes up by one per tick: 1000 per emulated second.
# 'sysbus.u54_1 PC' shows the hart running from the alias (0xFFFFFFC0_08...).
#
# DDR: each count writes count ^ 0xA5A5A5A55A5A5A5A to DDR at VA
# 0xFFFFFFC0_4000_0000 + (count * 1 MiB) mod 1 GiB, which the application's
# table maps to PA 0x10_0000_0000 + the same offset (Renode's stock platform
# has 1 GiB of DDR there). g_ddr_ok counts the words read back intact
# (= g_count), g_ddr_bad the others. Count 1000's word, for example:
#
#   sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x103E800000      -> 0x5A5A59B2
#   sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x103E800004      -> 0xA5A5A5A5
# A non-zero g_m_fault (M-mode shim: unexpected trap) means the hart parked;
# a PC at s_park's physical address means S-mode faulted before FreeRTOS
# started (e.g. a page table without the alias).

$elf?=@build/hello.elf

mach create "hello"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/cpus/polarfire-soc.repl
sysbus LoadELF $elf
sysbus.e51 IsHalted true
sysbus.u54_2 IsHalted true
sysbus.u54_3 IsHalted true
sysbus.u54_4 IsHalted true
sysbus.u54_1 PC 0x08000000
sysbus.u54_1 SetRegisterUnsafe 10 1
